What is AI fluency?
Using AI in the most effective and efficient way, this helps preventing AI halucination and gives better response (very important)

Three ways of AI engagement with people
->Automation : You provide instructions and it gives reponses 
->Augmentation : Human + AI work together for execution
->Agents : Runs independently via humans single instruction 

The 4D framework:
->Delegation (Problem awareness and solving)
Thoughfully deciding what work do, either with AI or with yourself
For this, 
- One need to understand the goal or the problem properly
- Know whether AI can or can't accomplish certain task
- Decide how to divide/share the work between AI and yourself
- Understanding unique adv and disadv of the available options
- Wisely chosing the model
Its like having a clear vision and strategic choosing

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
->Description
A detailed, context-rich prompt/information that has to be shared to AI for better response
It information should be like,
- How the output should be
- How AI should approach in order to execute
- How AI should behave
- Explain tasks, ask questions, provide context, guide and interact 

Prompting techniques
- Formatting based on different AI systems for efficiency
- Understanding AI context window properly
- Experimentation, personal experience
- Its an iterative process, what works today may not work tomorrow (rely mostly on experimenting and refining constantly)
The steps are,
->Provide context
Be specific of what you want and why you want also who you are!

->Give examples
Provide samples to make sure that the desired output looks the same

->Specify output constraints
Clearly explaining how output should look by giving conditions (for the input)

->Breakdown complex tasks
Simplifying big works into small chunks and also solving it one by one and following an algorithm like a math problem (step by step)

->Give AI space to think
This helps in the places that (you) missed out (two people think more efficient)

->Define roles
Getting the response (explanation) based on who you are (profession)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
->Discernment (Quality filter)
Since AI is over-confident even if the response is wrong, human common sense comes to play
Is the output usefull,factually accurate,well structured and meets the expectations?, 
Did it use the right approach?, 
Did it behave in right way? (aggressive or passive),
Is the interaction effiecient?,
Is it appropriate to the right audience?

- One needs good domain expertise to verify correctness
- Feedback: Discernment and Description loop

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
->Dilligence (Responsibility sheild)
Someone asks for a sensitive information (sent or received) or asking for an important decision from AI,
- Verification?, ensuring accuracy
- Honesty and Transparency
- Ethical use and critical awareness
- Creditability

Follow these 4Ds while asking anything from AI
